            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for closeness, then the Marathi for beloved."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: अपमान",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अपमान — apmān — \"an insult; humiliation\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सगळ्यांसमोर झालेला अपमान तो विसरला नाही. sagḷyāṁsamor jhālelā apmān to visarlā nāhī. He did not forget being humiliated in front of everyone."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अपमान (apmān) करणे, to insult; अपमान (apmān) होणे, to be humiliated."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अपमान (apmān) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit apamāna, \"disrespect, disgrace\" (CDIAL 433)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
